{"name":"Naxos Sky","hex":"#5dc2db","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Naxos","blocks":[{"text":"Naxos is a Greek island belonging to the Cyclades island group. It is the largest island in the group. The largest town and capital of the island is Chora or Naxos City, with 8,897 inhabitants out of the total 20,578 in the island. The main villages are Filoti, Apiranthos, Vivlos, Agios Arsenios, Koronos and Glynado. It was an important centre during the Bronze Age Cycladic Culture and in the Ancient Greek Archaic Period. The island is famous as a source of emery, a rock rich in corundum, which until modern times was one of the best abrasives available."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Naxos_%CE%9D%CE%AC%CE%BE%CE%BF%CF%82_2020-08-20_02_Chora_Grotta_and_Vintzi_beaches.jpg/330px-Naxos_%CE%9D%CE%AC%CE%BE%CE%BF%CF%82_2020-08-20_02_Chora_Grotta_and_Vintzi_beaches.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naxos","wikidata":"Q188527"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/20210713_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CF%81%CF%84%CE%AC%CF%81%CE%B1_6749.jpg/500px-20210713_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CF%81%CF%84%CE%AC%CF%81%CE%B1_6749.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/20210713_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CF%81%CF%84%CE%AC%CF%81%CE%B1_6749.jpg/1280px-20210713_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CF%81%CF%84%CE%AC%CF%81%CE%B1_6749.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/20210713_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CF%81%CF%84%CE%AC%CF%81%CE%B1_6749.jpg/500px-20210713_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CF%81%CF%84%CE%AC%CF%81%CE%B1_6749.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A20210713_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CF%81%CF%84%CE%AC%CF%81%CE%B1_6749.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Glezos_Tower.jpg/500px-Glezos_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Glezos_Tower.jpg/1280px-Glezos_Tower.jpg